<title>USA: Texaco Q1 beats estimates.</title>
<headline>Texaco Q1 beats estimates.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco first quarter operating earnings per share rose to $1.84 in the first quarter of 1997 from $1.42 a year ago and beat average analysts' forecasts of $1.72.</p>
<p>The stock, which had traded as high as 106 in early morning trade, fell back to 105-1/4, up 7/8 at late morning.</p>
<p>Texaco said on Monday that it would book a $488 million extraordinary gain due to a tax refund from the Internal Revenue Service in the first quarter.</p>
<p>It reported total net income per share of $3.72.</p>
</text>
